@export What is my Virginia taxable income (Va. Code ss 58.1-322, 58.1-325)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc single, married filing jointly, or married filing separately
      `my residence` IS A `Residence` @desc Whether you were a Virginia resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the taxable year begins in, for example 2026
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income in US dollars (joint, if married filing jointly)
      `my Virginia additions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total, in US dollars, of income Virginia adds back under s 58.1-322.01; 0 if none
      `my Social Security benefits in federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Social Security (Title II) benefits included in your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my other Virginia subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc Other income Virginia subtracts under s 58.1-322.02, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `I itemise on my federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you itemise deductions on your federal return
      `my federal itemised deductions less income taxes` IS A NUMBER @desc If you itemise: your federal itemised deductions minus income taxes deducted, in US dollars
      `someone can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another taxpayer may claim you as a dependent
      `my earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earned income in US dollars (used only if someone can claim you as a dependent)
      `my federal personal exemptions` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of personal exemptions allowable to you for federal purposes
      `my aged or blind additional amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc How many s 63(f) aged-or-blind additional amounts you (and your spouse) have
      `my child and dependent care expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The employment-related expenses your federal child and dependent care credit is based on, in US dollars
      `people on the return born on or before 1 January 1939` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people on the return were born on or before 1 January 1939
      `other people on the return aged 65 or over` IS A NUMBER @desc How many others on the return were born after 1 January 1939 and are 65 or older
      `my other Virginia deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of other deductions you take under s 58.1-322.03, in US dollars
      `my share of income from Virginia sources` IS A NUMBER @desc For a nonresident: Virginia-source net income over all net income (0 to 1); enter 1 otherwise
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my Virginia taxable income` `my filing status` `my residence` `the taxable year` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Virginia additions` `my Social Security benefits in federal AGI` `my other Virginia subtractions` `I itemise on my federal return` `my federal itemised deductions less income taxes` `someone can claim me as a dependent` `my earned income` `my federal personal exemptions` `my aged or blind additional amounts` `my child and dependent care expenses` `people on the return born on or before 1 January 1939` `other people on the return aged 65 or over` `my other Virginia deductions` `my share of income from Virginia sources` MEANS
    `the Virginia taxable income of` (`the Virginia taxpayer with` `my filing status` `my residence` `the taxable year` `my federal adjusted gross income` `my Virginia additions` `my Social Security benefits in federal AGI` `my other Virginia subtractions` `I itemise on my federal return` `my federal itemised deductions less income taxes` `someone can claim me as a dependent` `my earned income` `my federal personal exemptions` `my aged or blind additional amounts` `my child and dependent care expenses` `people on the return born on or before 1 January 1939` `other people on the return aged 65 or over` `my other Virginia deductions` `my share of income from Virginia sources`)

§§ `What credit do I get?`

@export Which credit for low-income taxpayers or earned income credit do I get, and how much (Va. Code s 58.1-339.8)?
GIVEN `the taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the taxable year begins in, for example 2026
      `my residence` IS A `Residence` @desc Whether you were a Virginia resident all year, a part-year resident, or a nonresident all year
      `people on my return` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the return covers: you, your spouse if married, and each dependent you claim
      `our family Virginia adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc The combined Virginia adjusted gross income of you, your spouse and your dependents, in US dollars
      `the poverty guideline for a household our size` IS A NUMBER @desc The HHS poverty guideline published in the taxable year for a household of that many people (48 contiguous states and DC), in US dollars
      `my federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER @desc The federal earned income credit (s 32) you claim for the year, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `we claim an item that bars the credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, your spouse or a dependent claims the age deduction, the extra $800 aged-or-blind exemption, the National Guard subtraction, or the s 58.1-322.02(15) or (16) subtraction
      `my Virginia income tax` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Virginia income tax for the year before this credit, in US dollars
GIVETH A `Credit`
`Which Virginia low-income or earned income credit do I get` `the taxable year` `my residence` `people on my return` `our family Virginia adjusted gross income` `the poverty guideline for a household our size` `my federal earned income credit` `we claim an item that bars the credit` `my Virginia income tax` MEANS
    `the s 58.1-339.8 credit` `the taxable year` `my residence` `people on my return` `our family Virginia adjusted gross income` `the poverty guideline for a household our size` `my federal earned income credit` `we claim an item that bars the credit` `my Virginia income tax`
